              "type": "text",
              "text": "<h3>Overview</h3><p><br></p><p>Join this practical five-week course to build confidence with money, strengthen your financial resilience and take greater control of your everyday finances.</p><p>You do not need to be “good with money”, good at maths or have any previous financial knowledge. Led by certified Financial Educator <strong><strong>Anna Orenstein-Cardona</strong></strong>, the course offers a supportive, non-judgemental environment where you can ask questions, develop practical skills and make financial decisions with greater confidence.</p><p><br></p><h3>Course Description</h3><p>Over five weeks, you will explore how your experiences and attitudes can shape the way you manage money, before moving on to practical topics including budgeting, spending, borrowing, debt, saving and investing.</p><p>The course will help you understand your current financial situation, identify realistic ways to strengthen it and develop an action plan for the future. You will also learn about credit, pensions, ISAs, common savings and investment options, and ways to protect yourself from financial scams.</p><p><br></p><h3>By the end of the course, you will be able to:</h3><ul><li>Recognise how your experiences and beliefs about money can influence your financial habits and decisions.</li><li>Understand the key areas of income, expenses, tax, debt and savings, and identify practical ways to improve your finances.</li><li>Create a realistic money plan based on your income, spending and priorities.</li><li>Understand borrowing costs, credit and practical approaches to managing debt.</li><li>Explain the main differences between saving and investing and recognise common savings, investment, pension and ISA options.</li><li>Create a personal action plan to continue improving your financial wellbeing.</li></ul>",
